          "why_linear_steer_fails": "The canonical debias baseline IS the content-gated linear steer: projecting out the gender subspace / occupation-gender direction (Bolukbasi/INLP-style). That destroys gender content everywhere it appears — breaking legitimate gendered coreference ('Mary said that ___', 'The actress … she') and gendered fact recall — which is exactly the documented collateral of linear debiasing. FRA cuts only the occupation×pronoun-slot pairing; gender features stay intact for every non-stereotype use. The legit-content KL panel writes itself: held-out sentences with explicitly gendered antecedents.",
