          "mechanism": "A loop is a self-conjunction — exactly the induction gate applied to the model's own output: (query = current token X inside the loop phrase) × (key = token-after-previous-X). Published analyses tie loop self-reinforcement to in-context copying (Xu et al. 2022 'Learning to Break the Loop'; repetition-neuron work), and the induction edge is the program's best-mapped FRA territory. Cut the top induction-head pairs for the looping n-gram once a loop is detected — content-addressed, so it follows the phrase wherever it recurs.",
          "why_linear_steer_fails": "The deployed fix — repetition/frequency penalty — is literally a content-gated steer on the repeated tokens' logits: it damages legitimate reuse (named entities, technical terms, anaphora that MUST repeat), a well-documented quality cost. FRA cuts only the copy EDGE: the token remains fully available whenever it is re-derived rather than copied. Risk to flag honestly: MLP repetition neurons may sustain loops after the edge is cut (a direct-consumption / redundancy failure), which is what the LBNR screen will catch first.",
