          "mechanism": "Finlayson et al. 2021 (causal mediation of syntactic agreement, GPT-2) show agreement at the verb position is mediated by attention from the verb-slot query (about-to-emit-verb syntactic features) to the subject head-noun key (number features), with attractor nouns competing as rival keys. That is a clean two-key conjunction structure: (verb-slot query content) × (subject-number key content) vs the same query × attractor key — FRA can edit the two competing cells DIFFERENTIALLY, which no other tool can.",
          "why_linear_steer_fails": "Steering the number direction (boost plural / suppress singular) changes number everywhere — every noun, the verb morphology itself, downstream pronouns — destroying agreement globally to fix it locally; the steer cannot favor the subject's number feature over the attractor's because they are the SAME feature at different keys, distinguished only by which query×key pair they sit in. The pair edit is the unique instrument that addresses 'this number feature, as read by the verb slot from THIS noun'.",
