      "notes": "METHOD: Consolidated 22 brainstormed entries into ~17 distinct behaviors, ranked against the repo's OWN validated ground truth (read from experiments/fra_win/: summary.md, FRA_PRINCIPLE.md, CAMPAIGN_REPORT.md, RESEARCH_LOG.md). Confirmed wins to anchor on: induction 15-235x; in-context backdoor flip (FRA 0.07 vs DoM 1.83 / conv-SAE 6.06); retrieval ~1100x (legit-frog KL 0.0016 vs steer 1.77); copy-suppression L10H7 R=0.95 A=22.7x; acronym R=0.95 A=38x. Confirmed LOSSES: IOI j13 R=-0.39 (backup name-movers, logit-diff moved only 0.17); fact-recall load-bearing (R=0.86) but base P(Paris)=0.039 too weak. CRITICAL repo finding: the s5 corpus-reuse magnitude-law attempt FAILED (attention-sink feature 15887 fired rate 1.00 on every edge -> degenerate denominator); the validated predictor is purely CCF-high AND LBNR-R-high, and 'common marginal' as a single-forward-pass number does NOT hold - separability is a cross-context/behavioral property. This is why the within-prompt-sibling designs (MQAR rank 3) are uniquely valuable: they fix the degenerate denominator and recover the A(N) magnitude law the program lacks.\n\nDOWN-RANKED / EXCLUDED FROM SHORTLIST (with reason):\n- Occupational gender-pronoun bias (Vig 2020): predicted LOSE/uncertain. CCF high but LBNR triple-risk: Vig's own result is SYNERGISTIC (attention AND neurons), L4-5 heads sit in the name-mover/IOI-backup family (j13 R=-0.39 prior), and the she/he decision plausibly reads aggregated gender from the residual (direction-routed, INLP's territory). Largest separability payoff IF it survives, but most likely a clean LBNR kill -> run only as a cheap screen-first, not a GPU commitment now.\n- WinoBias 2-entity anaphora + Colored-objects binding: differential-cell EXPRESSIVITY is genuinely FRA-unique, but both are name-mover/copy tasks -> IOI-backup LBNR risk is the gating failure (lean lose unless backups co-cut). Hold pending the knowledge-conflict result, which is the cheaper resolution of the same 'is LBNR-failure name-moving-per-se or IOI-task' question.\n- Bracket/quote matching: strongest LITERATURE LBNR signal (Dyck -0.967 vs -0.014 random) but that is a 2-layer toy trained-from-scratch; gpt2-small transfer is untested + quote TYPE detection is in an early MLP (direct-consumption risk). Promising but a research-grade feasibility gamble, not a now-bet.\n- Subject-verb agreement (plain): LOSE - direction-routed (arXiv 2310.15151 shows a ~1D linear agreement core that flips verb number; A->1, the sleeper failure mode). Agreement-under-ATTRACTOR (differential 2-key) is the salvageable FRA-unique variant (same number feature at two keys, only the pair distinguishes them) but resolution may be positional/syntactic; mid-tier, behind the retrieval cluster.\n- Pure LOSE controls (valuable as boundary-definers, cheap to co-run, NOT shortlist wins): IOI negative-name-mover (R<0.2, the calibrated negative twin of copy-suppression), parametric Geva fact-recall (distributed >150-head 'knowledge hub' + Hydra ~70% self-repair -> ROME/MEMIT is the right tool), duplicate-token dedup (redundant induction backup + downstream S-inhibition consumption). Recommend running IOI-neg + Geva alongside copy-supp/knowledge-conflict as the discriminator that LBNR (not CCF) is the gate.\n- gemma copy-suppression analog: gated on a head-discovery sub-task (no published gemma negative-head map) -> higher infra cost; do after the gpt2 corpus version confirms.\n\nSHORTLIST RATIONALE: the 5 picks are all (i) feasible NOW reusing existing harnesses (r2/g2-g4 for the three gemma retrieval cells; s3 for copy-supp; j13/ic for knowledge-conflict), (ii) predicted CCF^LBNR-pass with the strongest necessity arguments (context-only payload => attention-copy is the only route, for PII/MQAR/RAG; validated-anchor lift for copy-supp), (iii) on real/established benchmarks, and (iv) carry a genuine separability story where content is heavily reused so a linear steer must collateral. Priority order is PII (best CCF^LBNR + high importance) > copy-supp-corpus (de-risked validated lift) > MQAR (cheapest + fixes the magnitude law) > poisoned-RAG (high importance, slight two-step/held-out-collateral discount) > knowledge-conflict (highest-value/least-certain science, the L10H7-not-IOI test). All five share one cheap pre-flight: the LBNR position-patch / edge-cut screen BEFORE building FRA machinery - gate the GPU spend on it."
    }
